  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full 23-song set at the Showbox at the Market in Seattle on Monday, December 17, 2012 [1][2]. This concert was the final night of the Transcendental Youth tour [1]. The recording, captured by ∂®∑@Mßøä†, runs for 97 minutes and is the only available audio for this date [1]. The setlist opens with the Intro Song, which is the only archived performance of that track [1][2]. Other songs include White Cedar, Amy aka Spent Gladiator I, Love Love Love, Up the Wolves, Until I Am Whole, You or Your Memory, It Froze Me, Going to Port Washington, Peacocks, Steal Smoked Fish, Ezekiel 7 and the Permanent Efficacy of Grace, The Diaz Brothers, In Memory of Satan, Cry for Judas, The Mess Inside, First Few Desperate Hours, Spent Gladiator II, Transcendental Youth, This Year, Palmcorder Yajna, San Bernardino, and Best Ever Death Metal Band Out of Denton [1][2]. The performance of Peacocks is notable for being the first appearance of the song in 73 archived shows, a gap of 2,111 days, and it is one of only four archived performances [1][2]. During the show, John provided poignant introductions to both Until I Am Whole and In Memory of Satan [1]. The band was also joined by the brass and saxophone section that had previously recorded Transcendental Youth [1]. This is the 183rd show in the archive's collection for the band, following a performance at The Fillmore on December 14, 2012 [2].",
